      "keyInsight": "The people who get the worst back spasms are almost never slackers. They are the ultra-responsible perfectionists, the reliable helpers, and the relentless go-getters. On the outside, you present a calm, bulletproof face to the world. You hit every deadline, never complain, and keep the peace at family dinners. But deep inside, a primitive emotional boiler is rattling its iron lid. It is furious about endless chores, relentless demands, and self-imposed standards. Your conscious self refuses to admit this irritation because good people do not throw tantrums. So the brain devises a clever bargain. It decides that a stiff neck or a crippled lower back is far safer than an emotional explosion. Physical agony gives you an honorable excuse to rest without admitting you are overwhelmed.",
