      "keyInsight": "Ever wonder why a new massage or fancy back brace feels heavenly for two weeks, only for the pain to roar back later? It is the classic placebo trap. When you try an expensive gadget, your brain expects sweet relief. In response, it temporarily eases up on the choke collar. But because the underlying emotional boiler was never vented, the brain eventually finds a new spot to pinch. Chasing quick physical fixes is like painting over water damage on drywall without fixing the leaking roof pipe.",
