      "headline": "The Great Unity: How Your Feelings Steer Your Flesh",
      "keyInsight": "We love pretending the neck is a concrete border wall. The brain stays up in headquarters doing math and fretting about bills. The body stays downstairs hauling groceries and pulling weeds. When something aches in the basement, we blame bad floorboards or crooked lifting posture. But medicine made a colossal blunder by splitting the machine in two. Your body does not possess an independent nervous system detached from your emotional storms. Every secret worry dial cranks a tiny physical valve. When raw emotion boils over, the brain refuses to spill tears in public. Instead, it hits a hidden circuit breaker and tightens blood flow to a lower back muscle. The back spasm is not a mechanical defect like a dented car fender. It is an ingenious smokescreen engineered by a protective brain. The physical agony looks completely structural, yet its fuel tank sits entirely in your hidden feelings.",
